{"Origin check uses substring - accepts any sender origin that appears inside discourseUrl instead of requiring exact origin equality, allowing messages from wrong ports or dropping legitimate resize messages": 0.8777796030044556, "Feed items require content - many valid RSS/Atom entries provide summary, description, or only link/title instead of content, causing NoMethodError on i.content.scrub and aborting the whole scheduled poll": 0.9477090835571289, "Imported HTML skips sanitization - stores external article/feed HTML with raw_html cook_method, bypassing normal sanitizer and post-cook filters, creating stored XSS vulnerability when feed items contain script tags or event handlers": 0.9834939241409302, "Redirects escape host check - fetch happens after only initial embed URL host is checked, but open-uri follows redirects allowing allowed article URL to redirect to internal hosts like metadata or admin services": 0.9647135734558105, "Remote fetcher not loaded - import_remote uses open(url).read but file does not require open-uri and callers like TopicRetriever and Disqus task do not load it first, causing runtime failures": 0.8892986178398132, "Concurrent imports race condition - import path checks for existing embed_url then creates row without locking or rescuing unique-index conflict, causing request errors or dropped scheduled polls": 0.9337092041969299, "Embed stylesheet not precompiled - layout references standalone embed stylesheet but PR does not add embed.css to Rails asset precompile list, causing missing stylesheet or asset-not-precompiled error in production": 0.5457335710525513, "Missing slash breaks iframe URL - if discourseUrl is set without trailing slash, concatenation produces malformed URL like https://forum.example.comembed/best causing embed to never load": 0.8882402777671814, "Disqus links fetch arbitrary hosts - importer fetches t[:link] from Disqus XML without scheme or host validation, allowing modified export to make import task request internal HTTP services": 0.9098469614982605}